Subject: [202605] Initialize AS7326 and AS7726 IDT clocks before binding PDDF muxes

Backport the AS7326 ordering fix from PR #30498 and apply the same
ordering to AS7726, whose equivalent IDT init script directly opens its
mux addresses before PDDF takes ownership (0x76 rather than 0x70). No forced I2C writes,
clock register changes or AS5835/AS7816 ordering changes are introduced.
Reference: https://github.com/sonic-net/sonic-buildimage/pull/30498

Verified source: 5ef9e45ccf7f004fb07bf3f9be2f471cf00573bf.
Remove individual fixes when upstream supplies equivalent behavior.
Software regressions cover these changes; only AS7326 has been
inspected live. Other models require installation/hardware validation.

--- a/platform/broadcom/sonic-platform-modules-accton/as7326-56x/service/as7326-platform-handle_mac.service
+++ b/platform/broadcom/sonic-platform-modules-accton/as7326-56x/service/as7326-platform-handle_mac.service
@@ -1,7 +1,8 @@
 [Unit]
 Description=Accton AS7326-56X Platform MAC handle service
-Before=opennsl-modules.service
+Before=opennsl-modules.service pddf-platform-init.service
 After=local-fs.target
+DefaultDependencies=no
 
 [Service]
 Type=oneshot
--- a/platform/broadcom/sonic-platform-modules-accton/as7726-32x/service/as7726-32x-platform-handle_mac.service
+++ b/platform/broadcom/sonic-platform-modules-accton/as7726-32x/service/as7726-32x-platform-handle_mac.service
@@ -1,7 +1,8 @@
 [Unit]
 Description=Accton AS7726-32X Platform MAC handle service
-Before=opennsl-modules.service
+Before=opennsl-modules.service pddf-platform-init.service
 After=local-fs.target
+DefaultDependencies=no
 
 [Service]
 Type=oneshot
